  "verbalization": "The compound in question, a complex naphtho[2,1-f][1]benzofuran derivative, is implicated in the interaction with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 (UGT2B4) through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target of two different drugs, Mycalenitrile 13 and Ertugliflozin, both of which are known to interact with the Interferon alpha/beta receptor (IFNAR). This indicates that the compound may influence the function of IFNAR, potentially modulating signaling pathways that are involved in immune responses and cellular metabolism. The presence of multiple targets, including IFNAR and UGT2B4, suggests a possible mechanism by which the compound affects UGT2B4 activity, possibly through indirect interactions involving the IFNAR receptor. The evidence is consistent with a role for this compound in modulating UGT2B4 function, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
